irst insurance + 5 fee; block applies)\n10. 4 runes -> premium 115 G (no block — block requires exactly 3)\n11. 7 runes -> premium 198 G (no block)\n12. 2 runes + 1 moonstone -> premium 88 G (no block: different types)\n13. 3 runes + 3 moonstones -> premium 137 G (two separate blocks)\n14. cursed sword (0 years, 0 contracts) -> premium 165 G (100 base + 50 cursed + 10 first insurance + 5 fee)\n15. cursed sword + plain amulet (0 years, 0 contracts) -> premium 231 G\n16. sword enchantment 5 (0 years, 0 contracts) -> premium 145 G\n17. sword enchantment 4 (0 years, 0 contracts) -> premium 115 G (no high-enchantment)\n18. cursed sword enchantment 5 -> premium 195 G (both surcharges apply)\n19. customer with exactly 2 years, sword -> premium 95 G (loyalty discount applies)\n20. customer with 1 year, sword -> premium 115 G (no loyalty since 1 < 2)\n21. first insurance always applies: 5 years, 5 contracts -> premium 80 G\n22. follow-up contract adds 15 % discount: 5 years, 1 contract -> premium 80 G\n23. premium calculation yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up)\n24. unknown item type -> throws an error\n25. regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -> payout 400 G\n26. damage to a rune, damage 200 G -> payout 100 G\n27. dragon-material sword enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (50% wins, then deductible)\n28. dragon-material sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (both clauses, 50% wins)\n29. dragon-material sword enchantment 5, damage 800 G -> payout 700 G (only dragon clause applies)\n30. steel sword enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -> payout 400 G (only high-enchantment)\n31. damages insured sword (500 G) and insured amulet (300 G) -> payout 600 G (deductible once per item)\n32. sword + amulet policy -> insurance sum 1600 G, cap 3200 G\n33. cursed sword -> cap 2000 G (based on unmodified insurance value)\n34. sword + 3-rune block -> insurance sum 1750 G\n35. sword policy (cap 2000 G); first claim 1500 G -> payout 1400 G, remainin